## 2. Progress Checklist & Completed Tasks

### A. HelloWorld Project Verification
* Code Analysis: main.c has been reviewed. It prints log statements to both the USB DIAG port and direct USB Serial (COM24) and implements callback echo testing on COM24.
* GPIO Configuration: Configured `INDICATOR_GPIO_ID` to `7` in `main.c` to drive the general-purpose GPIO 7 (physical Pin 21 `GPIO_07` / `MAIN_DSR`). Using Pin 21 avoids the CP modem core conflict and system resets caused by hijacking `MAIN_RI` (`GPIO 4`).
* Compilation & Packaging: Run and completed the build_HelloWorld.bat script successfully.
* Output Artifacts: 
  * Compiled ELF/MAP files generated in SDK out/bin.
  * Flashable firmware package generated successfully at: E:\projects\DevelopmentLevelCode\Neoway_N706B\Code\HelloWorld\release\nwy_open_app.zip.
  * Interactive Pin Map Visualizer dashboard: E:\projects\DevelopmentLevelCode\Neoway_N706B\Code\N706B_Module_Pin_Map.html.

