## 4. Testing & Flashing Steps

To begin testing the HelloWorld application:
1. Hardware Setup:
   * Connect the Neoway N706B development board to the PC via USB and power it on.
2. Download Mode:
   * Connect to the board using a serial terminal on the AT port.
   * Send the command: AT$MYDOWNLOAD=1 to switch the board into download mode.
3. Flashing:
   * Open the Aboot tool located at: E:\projects\Devolapment files\Neoway\N706B-A07-STD-OE_CN1X_ITRI-009.zip\aboot-tools-2024.10.12-win-x64.exe\aboot-tools-2024.10.12-win-x64.exe\aboot-tools-2024.10.12-win-x64\aboot.exe (or your local extracted copy).
   * Select the package: E:\projects\DevelopmentLevelCode\Neoway_N706B\Code\HelloWorld\release\nwy_open_app.zip
   * Click Start to flash the code onto the module.
4. Verifying Outputs:
   * Direct COM Output: Open a serial terminal (like PuTTY or Tera Term) and connect to the USB Serial COM port representing COM24 (or the OpenCPU COM port). You should see:
     Hello World from Neoway N706B OpenCPU via COM24! Count: <n>, GPIO: <state>
     toggling every 1 second.
   * Echo Test: Send text data via the terminal to the COM24 port. The HelloWorld code is configured to echo it back to the terminal.
   * Binary Log Output: Open CoolWatcher/Log Tool to monitor the binary debug logs (NWY_SDK_LOG_DEBUG).
   * Version Verification: Send AT+NAPPCHECK? to check the current running version ("HelloWorld_V1.0.0").
